# business-game

C++23 SFML 2D scaffold: empty window loop, no gameplay yet. Do not assume menu, Arkanoid, or board-game features exist.

## Stack

- C++23, CMake ≥ 3.20, Ninja presets (`debug` / `release`)
- SFML 3.1 via FetchContent (`cmake/FetchSFML.cmake`) — Graphics/Window/System only; no manual SFML install
- GoogleTest 1.18 only in Debug; clang-format / clang-tidy at repo root

## Layout

- `src/main.cpp` — constructs `Game` and calls `run()`
- `src/Game.hpp` / `Game.cpp` — 1280×720 window, poll `Closed`, clear/display
- `tests/unit_tests/` — `smoke_test` (Debug)

Static library target: `gameLib`. Executable: `game`.

## Build / test

```sh
cmake --preset debug
cmake --build --preset debug --target game
cmake --build --preset debug --target build_ut
ctest --preset debug
```

Binary: `build/<preset>/bin/game` (`.exe` on Windows).

## Agent pitfalls

- New `.cpp` files must be listed in `src/CMakeLists.txt` (`gameLib`)
- Prototype snapshot: git branch `v0.1-arkanoid` (not this tree)
- Screen transitions / entities / ResourceManager are not present
